-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_optimize_override.pcpp - pcpp: -opt over @optimize

  A cli test: pcpp runs itself with the args (in the suite's output root,
  -o "$P:output" so the build lands there), on the fixture named; its
  output and exit code are the check. pcpp -opt is an override: it wins over the source's @optimize
  fast, so the program is a debug build (the runtime's heap report).
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_optimize_override;

/*
  @@test
    kind cli
    args "--no-banner <DIR>/fixtures/dir_cli_fast.pcpp -opt debug -r -o $P:output"
    exitcode 0
    expect
    | Compiling <DIR>/fixtures/dir_cli_fast.pcpp
    | Target platform: x86_64-windows-gnu
    | Optimize level: debug
    | Subsystem: Console
    | Saving build file...
    | Building dir_cli_fast...
    | Build succeeded.
    | Output: <OUT>/bin/dir_cli_fast.exe
    | Running dir_cli_fast.exe...
    | dir_cli_fast runs
    | [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  @@end
*/

begin
end.
